  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-1)! & =(n-1)(n-2)!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(n-2)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)!}{(n-2)!} & =\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!}{(n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n-1)^{2}\\cdot (n-1)\\cancel{(n-2)!}}{\\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =(n-1)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
